{
  "abstract": "We present evidence for \u03b4 production in the reactions K \u2212 p\u2192 \u03a3 (1385) + \u03b4 \u2212 ; \u03b4 \u2212 \u2192 \u03b7 0 \u03c0 \u2212 , and K \u2212 p \u2192 \u039b\u03b4 + \u03c0 \u2212 ; \u03b4 + \u2192 \u03b7 0 \u03c0 + , in a bubble chamber experiment with beam momentum in the range 3.1 to 3.6 GeV/ c . The \u03b7 0 from the \u03b4 decay is seen both as a missing mass effect, and in its charged decay modes. The \u03b4 \u2212 has a mass of 989 \u00b1 4 MeV, and width a of 16 \u221216 +25 MeV (after allowing for experimental resolution). The cross section for \u03a3(1385) \u2212 \u03b4 \u2212 production is 7\u00b13 \u03bc b; the reaction is produced at small momentum transfers. The mass and width of the \u03b4 + are consistent with those of the \u03b4 \u2212 , and the cross section for the \u039b 0 \u03c0 \u2212 \u03b4 + final state is about 5 \u03bcb. Neither \u03b4 appears to be produced as a result of D 0 decay.",
